well brian for the first time since 2017  the immigration program daca will now be  open to new  applicants now it protects undocumented  immigrants brought  to this country as children from being  deported  eight news now reporter orco mana  explains what this could mean for  nevadans this means the trump  administration has to fully restore daca  an obama era initiative now  approximately one million undocumented  immigrants including thousands here in  nevada  could benefit from it new applications  for daca which stands for deferred  action for childhood arrivals  have not been accepted for about three  years but on friday a federal judge  ordered the u.s department of homeland  security  to take in applications for immigrants  who qualify daca shield certain people  who came to the u.s as children  from deportation which means they can  stay in the country  for two years subject to renewal the  judge also said approved applicants  should get work permits that last for  two years  and current daca recipients known as  dreamers can travel abroad and return to  america  there are currently more than 640 000  dreamers in the u.s  and according to the american  immigration council over 12 thousand  dreamers  lived in nevada as of march 2020 local  attorneys say  many more can now be helped we thought  that we would have to wait until  president-elect biden came into office  for uscis to start accepting those  applications but this order is making it  very clear  that uscis has to accept them so there's  no longer  there's no longer a waiting period it's  time to it's time to apply  requirements for daca eligibility  include having no serious criminal  convictions  arriving in the u.s before age 16 living  here since at least 2007  and earning an american high school  diploma ged  or serving in the military many are  calling this new order a victory for  dreamers but the fight isn't necessarily  over yet  a dhs spokesman says while the  department will comply with the decision  they are working with the justice  department on next steps to appeal  reporting in las vegas orca mana 8 news  now
 

